# Three facts, in one run. Counting invocations rather than timing: on a shared host a stopwatch
# measures the host, and this has to be true on a busy machine too.
#   1. a second compile with nothing changed does NOT fork ssc  (it forked twice before this work)
#   2. editing a .ssc source DOES fork it again
#   3. changing sscBackends DOES too — nothing under src/ moves, so a source-only cache key would
#      keep yesterday's targets and call them fresh
> resetCalls
> compile
> compile
> expectBuilds 1
> touchSource
> compile
> expectBuilds 2
# 4, not 3: two backends mean two `ssc build` invocations, one per target. The first run of this
# scenario expected 3 and the count said 4 — the expectation was wrong, not the plugin, and a
# counter is what made that distinguishable from a cache miss.
> set sscBackends := Seq("jvm", "js")
> compile
> expectBuilds 4
